        bodyEnglish: `Narrated by Salman al-Farsi (R.A), the Prophet ﷺ said: "No man bathes on Friday, purifies himself as much as he can, applies oil or perfume, then goes to the mosque without stepping over two people, prays what has been decreed for him, and remains silent when the Imam speaks, except that he is forgiven for what transpired between that Friday and the next." (Sahih al-Bukhari: 883)

Commentary: This comprehensive tradition specifies complete Friday decorum: personal hygiene, scent, courteous seating without disturbing others, and absolute silence during the sermon.`
